<div class="tab {{tabs.combat.cssClass}}" data-group="primary" data-tab="combat">

  {{! These values are kept by hand during play, so they are locked until asked for:
      a stray click should not quietly change what a character has left. }}
  <section class="panel">
    <h3 class="panel-title">
      Turn State
      <button type="button" class="edit-toggle {{#if combatEditMode}}active{{/if}}"
              data-action="toggleCombatEdit"
              data-tooltip="Unlock the turn state and action counts for editing">
        {{#if combatEditMode}}Done{{else}}Edit{{/if}}
      </button>
    </h3>

    <div class="turn-state">
      <div class="stat"
           data-tooltip="An Instant Maneuver cannot follow another Instant.">
        <em>Last was Instant</em>
        {{#if combatEditMode}}
        <input type="checkbox" name="system.lastManeuverWasInstant"
               {{#if system.lastManeuverWasInstant}}checked{{/if}}/>
        {{else}}
        <span>{{#if system.lastManeuverWasInstant}}Yes{{else}}No{{/if}}</span>
        {{/if}}
      </div>

      {{#if charging}}
      {{! While a charge is held, the rules close off most of what you could otherwise
          do - so it is said plainly rather than only discovered by being refused. }}
      <div class="stat stat-charging"
           data-tooltip="Until this is thrown you suffer Guard Down and cannot use another Attacking or Standard Maneuver.">
        <em>Charging</em>
        <span>{{charging.name}}<span class="stat-of">{{#if charging.profile}} &middot; {{charging.profile}}{{/if}} &middot; {{charging.charges}} charge{{#unless charging.one}}s{{/unless}}</span></span>
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#each marks as |mark|}}
      {{! Hyped, Analyzed - marks a Maneuver put on somebody. Not Combat Conditions: the
          entries that create them do not call them that, and the checklist below is the
          published ones. Said here because this is where the sheet says what you are in
          the middle of. }}
      <div class="stat stat-charging" data-tooltip="{{mark.description}}">
        <em>{{mark.name}}</em>
        <span>{{#if mark.stacking}}{{mark.stacks}}{{else}}yes{{/if}}</span>
        {{#if mark.note}}<i class="stat-note">{{mark.note}}</i>{{/if}}
      </div>
      {{/each}}

      {{#if inside}}
      {{! Inside somebody, from the Internal Attack Maneuver. Out of the Initiative Order
          until they burst out, which is a thing everyone at the table needs to see. }}
      <div class="stat stat-charging" data-tooltip="They lose 2(T) of Soak Value and Defense Value until you come back out. Burst out from the card that put you in there.">
        <em>Inside</em>
        <span>{{inside.name}}</span>
        <i class="stat-note">{{inside.note}}</i>
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if transfigured}}
      {{! What they were turned into by the Transfiguration Maneuver. The Condition is in
          the list above; this is the Item, which the rule needs by name for the rest of
          the Encounter - "for all intents and purposes, becomes that Item". }}
      <div class="stat stat-charging" data-tooltip="Turned into this until the end of the Combat Encounter. If the Item is destroyed or used up, they die - a Karma Point avoids dying and not being Defeated. Targeting them with the Transfiguration Maneuver turns them back.">
        <em>Turned into</em>
        <span>{{transfigured.item}}</span>
        <i class="stat-note">{{transfigured.note}}</i>
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if weather}}
      {{! What Battle Weathers count as for this character. A row of its own rather than
          part of a mark: it is a fact about them as they stand, whatever put it there. }}
      <div class="stat stat-charging" data-tooltip="{{weather.note}}">
        <em>Weather</em>
        <span>{{weather.tiers}} Tier{{#unless weather.one}}s{{/unless}} lower</span>
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if delayed}}
      {{! A Maneuver paid for and held back. Nothing watches for the trigger - it is in
          the player's own words and the table is what calls it - so what this row is for
          is having it written where everybody can read it. }}
      <div class="stat stat-charging"
           data-tooltip="Paid for and waiting. Use it from the card that announced it, as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver costing nothing. It lapses at the start of your next turn.">
        <em>Holding</em>
        <span>{{delayed.name}}</span>
        <i class="stat-note">on {{delayed.trigger}}</i>
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{! What is left this round over what the round gives you. Both refill when the
          round turns over, so the second number is the one that is yours to change. }}
      <div class="stat" data-tooltip="Standard Actions left this round, of what each round gives you">
        <em>Standard Actions</em>
        {{#if combatEditMode}}
        <input type="number" data-action-type="standard" value="{{system.actions.standard}}" min="0"/>
        {{else}}
        <span>{{actionsLeft.standard}}<span class="stat-of">/{{system.actions.standard}}</span></span>
        {{/if}}
      </div>

      <div class="stat" data-tooltip="Counter Actions left this round, of what each round gives you">
        <em>Counter Actions</em>
        {{#if combatEditMode}}
        <input type="number" data-action-type="counter" value="{{system.actions.counter}}" min="0"/>
        {{else}}
        <span>{{actionsLeft.counter}}<span class="stat-of">/{{system.actions.counter}}</span></span>
        {{/if}}
      </div>

      {{! Wear accrued within a Combat Round. Both clear when the round turns over. }}
      <div class="stat"
           data-tooltip="Attacking Maneuvers made this round. Each one after the third costs a stack, and each stack reduces your Strike Rolls by 1(bT).">
        <em>Attacks this round</em>
        {{#if combatEditMode}}
        <input type="number" name="system.attacksThisRound" value="{{system.attacksThisRound}}" min="0"/>
        {{else}}
        <span>{{system.attacksThisRound}}</span>
        {{/if}}
        <i class="stat-note">Dim. Offense {{system.diminishing.offense.stacks}} &middot; Strike -{{system.diminishing.offense.penalty}}</i>
      </div>

      {{! Two a Combat Round, and the count resets with the round like the one above. }}
      <div class="stat"
           data-tooltip="Absolute Attacks made this round. Two is the limit, and a third cannot be declared.">
        <em>Absolute Attacks</em>
        {{#if combatEditMode}}
        <input type="number" name="system.absoluteAttacksThisRound"
               value="{{system.absoluteAttacksThisRound}}" min="0"/>
        {{else}}
        <span>{{system.absoluteAttacks.used}}<span class="stat-of">/{{system.absoluteAttacks.max}}</span></span>
        {{/if}}
      </div>

      <div class="stat"
           data-tooltip="Each stack reduces your Dodge Rolls by 1. Gained per Attacking Maneuver aimed at you, unless you use the Defend Maneuver.">
        <em>Dim. Defense</em>
        {{#if combatEditMode}}
        <input type="number" name="system.diminishingDefense" value="{{system.diminishingDefense}}" min="0"/>
        {{else}}
        <span>{{system.diminishingDefense}}</span>
        {{/if}}
        <i class="stat-note">Dodge -{{system.diminishing.defense.penalty}} &middot; +{{system.diminishing.defense.perAttack}} per attack</i>
      </div>

      {{! Not a Combat Condition, though it stacks like one - and not per-round wear
          either: how long a stack lasts is decided by whatever applied it. }}
      <div class="stat"
           data-tooltip="Each stack costs you 1(bT) Life Points at the start of your turn. How long a stack lasts is decided by whatever applied it.">
        <em>Damage Over Time</em>
        {{#if combatEditMode}}
        <input type="number" name="system.dotStacks" value="{{system.dotStacks}}" min="0"/>
        {{else}}
        <span>{{system.dot.stacks}}</span>
        {{/if}}
        {{#if system.dot.stacks}}
        <i class="stat-note">-{{system.dot.total}} Life at the start of your turn</i>
        {{/if}}
      </div>

      {{! Not per-round wear like the two above: Super Stacks are held until something
          takes them away. Shown beside them because this is where the counters live. }}
      <div class="stat"
           data-tooltip="Muscle Penalty: 1(bT) off Strike and Dodge per stack, 1(bT) more at three. Solid Bulk: 1(bT) of Soak per stack. Massive Power: 1/4 of your Force Modifier on the Wound Rolls of Physical and Energy Attacks, per stack.">
        <em>Super Stacks</em>
        {{#if combatEditMode}}
        <input type="number" name="system.superStacks" value="{{system.superStacks}}"
               min="0" max="{{system.superStack.max}}"/>
        {{else}}
        <span>{{system.superStack.stacks}}<span class="stat-of">/{{system.superStack.max}}</span></span>
        {{/if}}
        {{#if system.superStack.stacks}}
        <i class="stat-note">Strike &amp; Dodge -{{system.superStack.musclePenalty}}
          &middot; Soak +{{system.superStack.solidBulk}}
          &middot; Wound +{{system.superStack.massivePower}}</i>
        {{/if}}
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  {{! Where the character stands, and what being there is costing them. }}
  <section class="panel">
    <h3 class="panel-title">
      Health Threshold
      {{#if threshold.pending.length}}
      <button type="button" class="edit-toggle" data-action="steadfastCheck"
              data-tooltip="Roll for the thresholds crossed. Crossing several at once fails all but the lowest automatically.">
        Steadfast Check
      </button>
      {{/if}}
    </h3>
    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="stat threshold-{{system.threshold.key}}">
        <em>Threshold</em><span>{{system.threshold.label}}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat" data-tooltip="Failed Steadfast Checks at or below your current threshold">
        <em>Failures</em><span>{{system.threshold.failures}}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat" data-tooltip="1(bT) per failed Steadfast Check, off Strike, Dodge and Wound">
        <em>Combat Rolls</em><span>-{{system.threshold.penalty}}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat" data-tooltip="Power Level + 1, less one per failure">
        <em>Stress Bonus</em><span>{{system.stressBonus}}</span>
      </div>
      {{#if stressDice}}
      {{! What the Test itself rolls, where something has changed it. Beside the number it
          is measured against, because the two are read together or not at all. }}
      <div class="stat stat-charging" data-tooltip="{{stressDice.note}}">
        <em>Stress Test</em><span>{{stressDice.written}}</span>
      </div>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Values used only in combat. -->
  <section class="panel">
    <h3 class="panel-title">
      Combat Rolls
      {{! Tier of Power Extra Dice ride on every one of these. }}
      <span class="panel-note">Rolled as 1d10{{#if system.dice.extra.formula}} + {{system.dice.extra.formula}}{{/if}} + the value</span>
    </h3>
    <div class="stat-grid">
      {{! Each of these says what it is made of, and what it will pick up on the way to
          the dice - Diminishing Offense, a Health Threshold, the Extra Dice - none of
          which is in the number, because none of it is true of a character rather than
          of a roll. }}
      <div class="stat"><em>Strike</em>
        <span data-tooltip-html="{{workings.strike}}">{{system.combat.strike}}</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><em>Dodge</em>
        <span data-tooltip-html="{{workings.dodge}}">{{system.combat.dodge}}</span></div>
      {{! Wound uses the Damage Attribute, which depends on the attack's Foundation. }}
      {{#each woundRolls as |wound|}}
      <div class="stat">
        <em>Wound &middot; {{wound.label}}</em>
        <span data-tooltip-html="{{wound.workings}}">{{wound.value}}</span>
      </div>
      {{/each}}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Dice that ride alongside the Base Die. -->
  <section class="panel">
    <h3 class="panel-title">
      Dice
      <span class="panel-note">Base Die: 1d10</span>
    </h3>
    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="stat" data-tooltip="Rolled alongside the Base Die. Grows with Tier of Power.">
        <em>Extra Dice</em>
        <span>{{#if system.dice.extra.formula}}{{system.dice.extra.formula}}{{else}}&mdash;{{/if}}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat" data-tooltip="Extra Dice granted by effects, one Category above the Tier of Power Extra Dice.">
        <em>Greater Dice</em>
        <span>{{system.dice.greater.formula}}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat" data-tooltip="Added on a critical. Skill rolls always use a flat 1d4 instead.">
        <em>Critical Dice</em>
        <span>{{system.dice.critical.formula}}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat" data-tooltip="Most Dice Categories an Extra Dice may be raised by: Base Tier of Power + 1. Energy Charges are exempt.">
        <em>Max Category Increase</em>
        <span>{{system.dice.maxCategoryIncrease}}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The most Ki that may be spent within one Combat Round. -->
  <section class="panel">
    <h3 class="panel-title">
      Capacity
      <span class="panel-note">Ki spendable per Combat Round</span>
    </h3>
    <div class="capacity">
      <div class="resource-card resource-capacity">
        <label>Spent this round</label>
        <div class="resource-values">
          <span class="computed-value">{{system.capacity.spent}}</span>
          <span class="resource-sep">/</span>
          <span class="computed-value">{{system.capacity.max}}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meter"><div class="meter-fill" style="width: {{capacityPercent}}%"></div></div>
      </div>
      <button type="button" data-action="resetCapacity" class="capacity-reset"
              data-tooltip="Give back the Actions and the Capacity, and clear the attacks made and the Diminishing stacks. A Combat does this on its own each round.">New round</button>
      <button type="button" data-action="resetEncounter" class="capacity-reset"
              data-tooltip="Restore maneuvers limited to once per encounter">New encounter</button>
      {{#if canEnterEncounter}}
      {{! For somebody who walked into an Encounter already under way: it began for
          everyone else when it began, and it begins for them now. Gone once taken, and
          back with the next Encounter. }}
      <button type="button" data-action="enterEncounter" class="capacity-reset"
              data-tooltip="The Combat Encounter begins for you now. Applies your start-of-Encounter effects, once.">Enter the encounter</button>
      {{/if}}
      <span class="capacity-note">{{system.capacity.remaining}} left this round</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  {{#if grapple}}
  {{! A Grapple holds two characters and each of them has half of it. The row says which
      half this one is, because most of the rules in the entry turn on that, and offers
      only the button that half has. }}
  <section class="panel dbu-grapple">
    <h3 class="panel-title">
      Grapple
      <span class="panel-note">
        {{#if grapple.grappler}}Grappler &middot; holding {{grapple.name}}
        {{else}}Grappled &middot; held by {{grapple.name}}{{/if}}
      </span>
    </h3>

    <p class="dbu-grapple-note">Guard Down for as long as it lasts, and it cannot be
      taken off while you are in it.</p>

    {{#if grapple.grappler}}
    <button type="button" data-action="releaseGrapple" class="capacity-reset"
            data-tooltip="End the Grapple. An Instant Maneuver, on your turn.">Let go</button>
    {{else}}
    {{! One Action, one Check. What the earlier attempts this turn bought shows beside
        it, since that is what decides whether another one is worth an Action. }}
    <button type="button" data-action="escapeGrapple" class="capacity-reset"
            data-tooltip="Spend 1 Action on a Grapple Check against the Grappler. Lose it and you can try again: every Action spent this turn raises the next Check by 1(T).">Escape</button>
    {{#if grapple.tried}}
    <span class="capacity-note">{{grapple.tried}} tried this turn &middot; next Check
      +{{grapple.nextBonus}}</span>
    {{/if}}
    <span class="capacity-note">{{grapple.actions}} Actions left this round</span>
    {{/if}}
  </section>
  {{/if}}

  {{! States. Entered by hand for the same reason Conditions are, and shown next to
      them because the two reference each other constantly in the rules. }}
  <section class="panel">
    <details class="condition-group" data-section="states"
             {{#if openSections.states}}open{{/if}}>
      <summary class="panel-title">
        States
        {{#if anyState}}
        <span class="panel-note">{{stateSummary}}</span>
        {{else}}
        <span class="panel-note">Normal</span>
        {{/if}}
      </summary>

      <ul class="condition-list">
        {{#each states as |state|}}
        <li class="condition {{#if state.active}}condition-active{{/if}}">
          <button type="button" class="condition-toggle" data-action="toggleState"
                  data-state="{{state.key}}" data-tooltip="{{state.text}}"
                  aria-pressed="{{#if state.active}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}">
            <span class="condition-mark">{{#if state.active}}&#10003;{{/if}}</span>
            <span class="condition-name">{{state.name}}</span>
          </button>

          {{#if state.levelled}}
          {{! Levels are not unlocks: at level 2 the level 1 effect is worth 2(T), so
              which level you are at changes every number the State gives. }}
          <span class="condition-stacks">
            <button type="button" class="stack-step" data-action="stepState"
                    data-state="{{state.key}}" data-step="-1"
                    data-tooltip="One level lower">&minus;</button>
            <span class="stack-count">{{state.level}}/{{state.levels}}</span>
            <button type="button" class="stack-step" data-action="stepState"
                    data-state="{{state.key}}" data-step="1"
                    data-tooltip="One level higher">+</button>
          </span>
          {{/if}}
        </li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>
    </details>
  </section>

  {{! Combat Conditions. Set by hand, because most of the ways one is inflicted are not
      things the system resolves - though an effect can set one too, and this shows it. }}
  <section class="panel">
    <details class="condition-group" data-section="conditions"
             {{#if openSections.conditions}}open{{/if}}>
      <summary class="panel-title">
        Combat Conditions
        {{#if anyCondition}}
        <span class="panel-note">{{conditionSummary}}</span>
        {{else}}
        <span class="panel-note">None</span>
        {{/if}}
      </summary>

      <ul class="condition-list">
        {{#each conditions as |condition|}}
        <li class="condition {{#if condition.active}}condition-active{{/if}}">
          <button type="button" class="condition-toggle" data-action="toggleCondition"
                  data-condition="{{condition.key}}" data-tooltip="{{condition.text}}"
                  aria-pressed="{{#if condition.active}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}">
            <span class="condition-mark">{{#if condition.active}}&#10003;{{/if}}</span>
            <span class="condition-name">{{condition.name}}</span>
          </button>

          {{#if condition.stacking}}
          {{! A stacking Condition needs a number, not a tick: Broken at three stacks is
              a different rule from Broken at one. }}
          <span class="condition-stacks">
            <button type="button" class="stack-step" data-action="stepCondition"
                    data-condition="{{condition.key}}" data-step="-1"
                    data-tooltip="One less stack">&minus;</button>
            <span class="stack-count">{{condition.stacks}}/{{condition.maxStacks}}</span>
            <button type="button" class="stack-step" data-action="stepCondition"
                    data-condition="{{condition.key}}" data-step="1"
                    data-tooltip="One more stack">+</button>
          </span>
          {{/if}}
        </li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>

      {{#if conditionAbilities}}
      {{! What a Condition lets you do about it: standing up from Prone, or clashing
          free of Pinned. Each costs the Actions its own effect asks for. }}
      <ul class="condition-abilities">
        {{#each conditionAbilities as |ability|}}
        <li>
          <button type="button" class="rollable" data-action="useConditionAbility"
                  data-source="{{ability.sourceId}}" data-block="{{ability.block}}"
                  {{#unless ability.affordable}}disabled{{/unless}}
                  data-tooltip="{{ability.tooltip}}">
            {{ability.label}}
          </button>
        </li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>
      {{/if}}
    </details>
  </section>

  {{! Everything with stacks on it, beside the two checklists above because it answers
      the same kind of question: not what this round is made of, but what you are
      carrying. The two Diminishing counters are here as well as in the Turn State panel -
      that one is where they are edited and where what each costs you is said, and this is
      where you count them with everything else. }}
  <section class="panel">
    <details class="condition-group" data-section="resources"
             {{#if openSections.resources}}open{{/if}}>
      <summary class="panel-title">
        Resources
        {{#if anyStacks}}
        <span class="panel-note">{{stackSummary}}</span>
        {{else}}
        <span class="panel-note">None</span>
        {{/if}}
      </summary>

      <ul class="condition-list dbu-stack-list">
        {{#each stacks as |row|}}
        <li class="condition {{#if row.stacks}}condition-active{{/if}}"
            data-tooltip="{{row.tooltip}}">
          <span class="condition-name">{{row.name}}</span>
          {{! A Resource with no ceiling says how many and nothing more: "3/0" would be
              a maximum of nothing rather than no maximum at all. }}
          <span class="stack-count">{{row.stacks}}{{#if row.max}}/{{row.max}}{{/if}}</span>
        </li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>

      {{#if anyStacks}}
      {{! What the ones that are doing something are doing, under the roll-call - the
          count alone says you have two of something and not what two costs. }}
      <ul class="condition-abilities dbu-stack-notes">
        {{#each stacks as |row|}}
        {{#if row.note}}
        <li><em>{{row.name}}</em> {{row.note}}</li>
        {{/if}}
        {{/each}}
      </ul>
      {{/if}}
    </details>
  </section>

  {{! Stand-ins for systems that do not exist yet, so the rules that depend on them
      can still be tried out. }}
  <section class="panel">
    <h3 class="panel-title">
      Debug
      <span class="panel-note">Manual stand-ins for unimplemented systems</span>
    </h3>
    <label class="debug-toggle"
           data-tooltip="From a Form entered through the Transformation Maneuver: Maximum Ki doubled, Max Capacity increased by half.">
      <input type="checkbox" name="system.debug.kiMultiplier"
             {{#if system.debug.kiMultiplier}}checked{{/if}}/>
      Ki Multiplier
      {{#if system.debug.kiMultiplier}}<em>Ki x2 &middot; Capacity x1.5</em>{{/if}}
    </label>
  </section>

</div>
